{#
	Twig port of mod_related_pages.html5. Flat legacy identifier
	`mod_related_pages` - see mod_pagepreview.html.twig for why there is no
	`.twig-root` marker and why the .html5 was deleted.

	The loop variable is `entry`, not `page`: `page` is a reserved-feeling name
	in a Contao Twig context and shadowing it here would be a trap for anyone
	extending this template later.

	pageTitle is the OPTIONAL meta override on tl_page and is empty on a stock
	page, so printing it alone rendered every entry as a link with no visible
	text. Core resolves this pair the same way round.

	Escaping: page_teaser was already escaped explicitly in the .html5 with
	StringUtil::specialchars(); autoescaping now does it, so the explicit call is
	gone rather than doubled. title/pageTitle/url are data and are escaped.
	page_image and page_images are <img> markup built by PageImageRenderer and
	stay |raw.

	The `<!-- indexer::stop -->` pair is kept here for the same reason as in
	mod_pagepreview.html.twig, and it needed deciding separately because this one
	is NOT a navigation module - RelatedPages extends \Contao\Module, so core's
	"navigation is not content" precedent does not carry it. The argument that does
	is the other one: this module renders other pages' teasers, so unwrapped it
	would make the hosting page win search hits that belong to the pages it links
	to. See mod_pagepreview.html.twig for the full note and for why this costs
	contao-zyppy-search nothing.
#}
<!-- indexer::stop -->
<nav class="{{ class }} block"{{ cssID|default('')|raw }}{% if style %} style="{{ style|raw }}"{% endif %}>

	{% if headline %}
		<{{ hl }}>{{ headline|raw }}</{{ hl }}>
	{% endif %}

	{% if pages|default([]) %}
	<div class="related_pages">
	{% for entry in pages %}
		<a href="{{ entry.url|default('') }}">
			<div class="related_page">
				<h6>{{ entry.pageTitle|default('') ?: entry.title|default('') }}</h6>
				{% if entry.page_image|default('') %}
					{{ entry.page_image|raw }}
				{% endif %}
				{% if entry.page_images|default([]) %}
					{% for image in entry.page_images %}
					{{ image|raw }}
					{% endfor %}
				{% endif %}
				{% if entry.page_teaser|default('') %}
					<span class="page_teaser">{{ entry.page_teaser }}</span>
				{% endif %}
			</div>
		</a>
	{% endfor %}
	</div>
	{% endif %}

</nav>
<!-- indexer::continue -->
